# Studio Testing Policy

The Studio is an Electron application. Integration tests spawn Electron windows that take over the user's screen while they work on other things.

## Rules

- **Ask first, every time.** Before running any Studio integration test, ask the user in chat and wait for an explicit yes. This applies to every run: the full suite, a single folder, a single file, and re-runs after a fix.
- **A plan is not permission.** An approved plan, a checklist step ("run the gate", "integration tests"), `do exe`, or an earlier yes in the same conversation does not count. Ask again right before running.
- **Unit tests are always allowed.** `npm run test:unit` runs without Electron and needs no permission.
- **NEVER** run bare `vitest run` / `npx vitest run` in `studio/`, and never call `vitest` on `test/integration/` directly. Use the npm scripts below, after the user has said yes.
- **Clean up.** If an integration run is still active when you no longer need it, or the user asks you to stop, terminate the whole process tree (vitest, chromedriver, Electron).

When asking, name the script and the suites it covers, and say roughly how long it takes.

## Available Test Scripts (defined in `studio/package.json`)

| Script | What it runs |
|--------|-------------|
| `npm run test:unit` | Unit tests only (`test/unit/`) — no Electron, always allowed |
| `npm run test:integration` | All integration suites (alias of `test:integration:all`) |
| `npm run test:integration:core` | `test/integration/studio-core/` |
| `npm run test:integration:bpmn-editor` | `test/integration/bpmn-editor/` |
| `npm run test:integration:dmn-editor` | `test/integration/dmn-editor/` |
| `npm run test:integration:git-cruiser` | `test/integration/git-cruiser/` |
| `npm run test:integration:plugins` | `test/integration/plugins/` (builds plugin fixtures first) |
| `npm run test:integration:smoke` | Smoke test only (single file) |

## After Code Changes

When verifying code changes in `studio/`:

1. `npm run build` — Compile bundles
2. `npm run lint:fix` — ESLint with auto-fix
3. `npm run format` — Prettier
4. `npm run test:unit` — Unit tests
5. Integration tests — **only after asking the user and getting a yes**
